265307+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "collector", "content": "{\"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.engappai.2022.104661\", \"error\": \"ValueError\", \"scope\": \"fetch failed; no evidence obtained\"}", "id": "source-1ef9390e9bfd41e2", "scope": "failed", "source": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.engappai.2022.104661"}, "prev_hash": "74879ac5342333e69acc8f57f6bdb57c6aa5b7be3c9aba9dce65d7317cb970cd", "hash": "42b029fa4765c88224bf5f32983d74ba38d970cb6d45b682c8a6cecdaf0a1291"}, {"seq": 723, "time": "2026-10-23T01:12:45.334367+00:00", "kind": "acquisition_assessed", "payload": {"domain": "unassigned_problem", "evidence": "source-9dd737e28fd049f6", "outcome": "routing_progress", "persistent_identifiers": ["doi:10.1016/j.engappai.2022.104661", "doi:10.62891/54fe0b5d", "doi:10.5220/0004628604070419", "doi:10.32628/ijsrset22962"], "project": "proj-autonomous-inquiry-001", "research_id": "immediate-c7451711dc4153c8", "route": "api.crossref.org:discovery", "source_candidate_identities": {}, "source_candidates": ["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.engappai.2022.104661", "https://doi.org/10.62891/54fe0b5d", "https://doi.org/10.5220/0004628604070419", "https://doi.org/10.32628/ijsrset22962"], "stage": "discovery"}, "prev_hash": "de85f356e55e529d801c3ec6893e767e5778b9fa2438d26fc5840ea067ba9f3e", "hash": "74879ac5342333e69acc8f57f6bdb57c6aa5b7be3c9aba9dce65d7317cb970cd"}, {"seq": 722, "time": "2026-10-23T01:12:43.239453+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "collector", "content": "{\"url\": \"https://api.crossref.org/works?query=mechanisms+for+autonomous+problem+formulation+and+scientific+curiosity+in+artificial+intelligence&rows=4&select=DOI%2Ctitle%2Cabstract%2CURL%2Cpublished\", \"scope\": \"Crossref bibliographic metadata and abstracts where supplied; not full papers\", \"excerpt\": \"[{\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.1016/j.engappai.2022.104661\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Problem formulation in inventive design using Doc2vec and Cosine Similarity as Artificial Intelligence methods and Scientific Papers\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.engappai.2022.104661\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2022, 3]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.62891/54fe0b5d\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"The Fifth Paradigm: Scientific Discovery in the Age of Autonomous Artificial Intelligence\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.62891/54fe0b5d\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2025, 7, 13]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.5220/0004628604070419\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Artificial Curiosity Emerging Human-like Behaviour - A Fundation for Fully Autonomous Cognitive Machines\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.5220/0004628604070419\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2013]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.32628/ijsrset22962\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Autonomous Intelligence in Problem-Solving by Searching in the field of Artificial Intelligence\\\"], \\\"abstract\\\": \\\"<jats:p>Problem-solving strategies in Artificial Intelligence are steps to overcome the barriers to achieve a goal, the \\\\\\\"problem-solving cycle\\\\\\\". Most common steps in such cycle involve- recognizing a problem, defining it, developing a strategy in order to fix it, organizing knowledge and resources available, monitoring progress, and evaluating the effectiveness of the solution. Once a solution is obtained, another problem usually comes, and the cycle starts again. Searching techniques in problem-solving by using artificial intelligence (A.I) are surveyed in this paper. An overview of definitions, development and dimensions of A.I in the light of search for solutions to problems are accepted. Dimensions as well as relevance of search in A.I research is reviewed. A classification of searching in the matter of depth of known parameters of search was also investigated. At last, the forethoughts of searching in AI research are brought into prominence. Search is noticed that it is the common thread that binds most of the problem-solving strategies in AI 